um", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Husted (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's special Senate race pits appointed incumbent Republican Jon Husted against former Senator Sherrod Brown in a state that has trended Republican in recent cycles. Brown has raised far more money and holds a large cash advantage, while Husted benefits from incumbency and supportive outside spending. Both sides are drawing national attention, with Trump campaigning for Husted and Obama stumping for Brown.\n\nPolling through early October consistently shows Brown narrowly ahead, with nonpartisan surveys giving him a 3-6 point edge and even Republican-leaning pollsters showing small Democratic leads. Prediction markets put Brown's chances near 60-65%, and several expert raters have shifted the race toward Democrats, though others still call it a tossup. The race remains genuinely competitive given Ohio's partisan lean and the incumbent's position.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7221, "margin": 2.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7246, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6986, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6393, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6851, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7568, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7432, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7463, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7417, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7438, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7437, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6872, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6759, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6875, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.716, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6739, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6435, "margin